lesson: 134
title: Metres and centimetres, dollars and cents
level: primary-2
stars: 0
explain: 1 metre is 100 centimetres, and 1 dollar is 100 cents.
explain: To write 3 metres 25 centimetres in centimetres, turn the metres into centimetres and add: 300 + 25 = 325 centimetres.
explain: Money works the same way: 4 dollars 60 cents is 400 + 60 = 460 cents.
vars: a=name b=name m=2..9 c=2..99
answer: 100 * m + c
exercise: A ribbon is {m} metres {c} centimetres long. How long is it in centimetres?
exercise: {a} has {m} dollars and {c} cents. How many cents is that?
exercise: A rope is {m} m {c} cm long. How many centimetres long is the rope?
exercise: {a} pays {m} dollars {c} cents for a book. How many cents does the book cost?
exercise: A path is {m} metres and {c} centimetres long. Write its length in centimetres.
exercise: {a} saved {m} dollars and {c} cents. How many cents did {a.he} save?
test: How many centimetres are there in {m} metres {c} centimetres?
test: {a}'s piggy bank holds {m} dollars and {c} cents in all. What is that in cents?
test: {b} measures a fence and finds it is {m} m {c} cm long. How many cm long is the fence?
test: A toy costs {m} dollars {c} cents. Give its price in cents only.
exercise: How many centimetres long is a scarf of {m} metres {c} centimetres?
exercise: {m} m {c} cm. How many cm is that?
exercise: In a shop in Boston, {a} spends {m} dollars and {c} cents. How many cents does {a.he} spend?
exercise: {a} has {m.words} dollars and {c.words} cents in {a.his} purse. How many cents is that in total?
exercise: A curtain in a house in Toronto is {m} metres {c} centimetres wide. What is its width in centimetres?
exercise: {a} found {c} cents and {m} dollars in {a.his} coat. How many cents is that altogether?
exercise: A banner for a school in Perth is {m} m and {c} cm long. How long is it in centimetres?
exercise: A comic book in Vancouver costs {m} dollars {c} cents. How many cents does it cost?
test: Write {c} cm and {m} m together as centimetres only.
test: {b} in New Zealand jumped {m} metres {c} centimetres. Give the jump in centimetres.
test: What is {m} dollars and {c} cents when it is counted in cents?
test: A rug in Ohio measures {m} metres {c} centimetres. Change that length into centimetres.
test: {a}'s pocket money comes to {m.words} dollars and {c.words} cents. How many cents is it?
test: A snake at a zoo in Queensland is {m} m {c} cm long. How many centimetres is that?
exercise: ribbon's {m} m {c} cm. how many cm is that
exercise: {a} got {m+1} dollars — no sorry, {m} dollars and {c} cents. in cents?
exercise: my cousin says {m} m {c} cm is {m+c} cm. nah. how many cm really
exercise: {a}'s rope is {m} metres {c} centimetres, it was 3 dollars at the shop. how long in cm
test: got {m} bucks {c} cents in me pocket, how many cents all up
test: {b} reckons {m} dollars {c} cents makes {10*m+c} cents. thats wrong yeah? how many cents
test: the plank's {m+1} metres — nah, {m} metres {c} cm. how long in centimetres
exam: It is given that a ribbon measures {m} metres and {c} centimetres in length. Determine its length expressed exclusively in centimetres.
exam: Whereas {a} is in possession of {m} dollars and {c} cents, ascertain the equivalent sum expressed in cents.
exam: A rope of length {m} m {c} cm is to be measured in a single unit. State its length in centimetres.
exam: Compute the number of centimetres in a length of {m.words} metres and {c} centimetres.
exercise: Grandma passed away and left {m} dollars and {c} cents in her old purse. How many cents did she leave?
exercise: Since Mum was let go, {a} counts the money in the jar carefully: {m} dollars and {c} cents. How many cents is that?
test: {b}'s "a little short" again, wants to borrow {m} bucks {c}. how many cents is that, bloody hell
